1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,308
Before investing in solar, one decision connects many questions.

2
00:00:05,588 --> 00:00:12,277
Is the roof suitable? What could it generate? And how might that investment perform?

3
00:00:12,557 --> 00:00:17,300
Signix brings those questions into one rooftop planning workspace.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:25,562
Begin with a dedicated Home planning experience, using the location and electricity
inputs for your scenario.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:34,648
The satellite map provides visual context. Draw a planning boundary, then mark the
areas you want to exclude.

6
00:00:34,928 --> 00:00:41,661
Here, a demonstration footprint and obstruction show how usable area changes before
sizing begins.

7
00:00:41,941 --> 00:00:46,915
This is an illustrative planning exercise, not a survey of this building.

8
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:52,973
The rooftop designer connects the footprint to a panel layout preview.

9
00:00:53,253 --> 00:01:01,486
Switch between views and inspect the arrangement. Prototype geometry and unverified
shade remain clearly identified.

10
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:09,623
Generation forecasts turn the selected system into monthly and long term energy
estimates.

11
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:14,326
The application exposes its data source and planning assumptions.

12
00:01:14,606 --> 00:01:23,824
This demonstration uses mock weather fallback. These figures illustrate the
calculation workflow, rather than verified site production.

13
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:33,203
For a home, review the estimated investment, household savings, and payback alongside
the assumptions behind them.

14
00:01:33,483 --> 00:01:39,291
Any residential assistance is indicative and subject to eligibility and official
verification.

15
00:01:39,571 --> 00:01:43,259
A planning estimate is never a guarantee of savings.

16
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:50,523
Business planning uses its own commercial policies while sharing the rooftop and
energy workflow.

17
00:01:50,803 --> 00:02:00,111
Review capital cost, the annual operations and maintenance reserve, net operating
benefit, return on investment, and payback.

18
00:02:00,391 --> 00:02:06,794
Residential subsidy is not a commercial benefit. Demand charge savings are not
modelled.

19
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:16,663
Save a configuration, change one planning choice, and compare the resulting scenarios
for the same roof.

20
00:02:16,943 --> 00:02:23,971
The side by side view makes differences in capacity, investment, and expected
performance easier to discuss.

21
00:02:24,251 --> 00:02:28,050
The calculation engine supplies the results shown here.

22
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:34,758
Export the planning summary for a conversation with an installer or project partner.

23
00:02:35,038 --> 00:02:41,771
Keep the assumptions and limitations with the figures, so the next decision starts
with the same context.

24
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:50,868
The same report can be explored in English and Hindi, helping more people participate
in the decision.

25
00:02:54,500 --> 00:03:00,903
Map the roof. Understand the energy potential. Compare the investment.

26
00:03:01,183 --> 00:03:05,137
Signix. Rooftop Solar Planning.

27
00:03:05,417 --> 00:03:12,540
Use the estimate to ask better questions, then verify the site, design, and approvals
before procurement.